Read water and sanitation from zero (@wu-reading: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @water-and-sanitation, #source "../sources/Manual-de-Saneamento-Funasa.lingua#r_65G5YY3QVCA8HAXMPC8RTPKEWE", #source "../sources/Introduction-to-Drinking-Water-Treatment-TU-Delft.lingua#r_0XXF9PBVKKD6FWSJRVDTCKQXP4", #source "../sources/Wastewater-Characteristics-Treatment-and-Disposal.lingua#r_59N8AH8ZNEKJK3HC4J32RV50XC", #water-and-sanitation "A-tap-a-drain-and-the-work-between-them.lingua#r_4BZY7VTHAE6B6WH956HKPZY906") { r_0KN6MHTA9SM9R7MK2CGT9KDJ35
**Read:** [Manual de Saneamento — Funasa, fifth edition](../sources/Manual-de-Saneamento-Funasa.lingua#r_65G5YY3QVCA8HAXMPC8RTPKEWE), chapters 1–5 in full, followed by the relevant construction, mapping and service chapters; [Introduction to Drinking Water Treatment — TU Delft](../sources/Introduction-to-Drinking-Water-Treatment-TU-Delft.lingua#r_0XXF9PBVKKD6FWSJRVDTCKQXP4), the entire introductory course; [Wastewater Characteristics, Treatment and Disposal — von Sperling](../sources/Wastewater-Characteristics-Treatment-and-Disposal.lingua#r_59N8AH8ZNEKJK3HC4J32RV50XC), the complete first wastewater volume.

Begin with a tap, a drain and a description of where their water comes from and goes. Draw the places and people involved before trying to size a treatment plant. A clear-looking liquid, a measured flow and a reliable service are three different observations.

Read chapters 1–5 of [Manual de Saneamento — Funasa, fifth edition](../sources/Manual-de-Saneamento-Funasa.lingua#r_65G5YY3QVCA8HAXMPC8RTPKEWE) in full and complete [Introduction to Drinking Water Treatment — TU Delft](../sources/Introduction-to-Drinking-Water-Treatment-TU-Delft.lingua#r_0XXF9PBVKKD6FWSJRVDTCKQXP4). Return to the shared quantitative, chemical and physical steps when the assigned reading first needs them. Work all of [Wastewater Characteristics, Treatment and Disposal — von Sperling](../sources/Wastewater-Characteristics-Treatment-and-Disposal.lingua#r_59N8AH8ZNEKJK3HC4J32RV50XC) and [Basic Principles of Wastewater Treatment — von Sperling](../sources/Basic-Principles-of-Wastewater-Treatment.lingua#r_083WF4FQEZQHB29YJBHWVZ0BEV) as wastewater becomes part of the same water-service account. These books supply sustained explanations and substantial problems beyond the connecting text here.

Develop treatment design through the whole [The Physics of Water Treatment Design — AguaClara](../sources/Physics-of-Water-Treatment-Design-AguaClara.lingua#r_1V2KMP22J5KMQF65K8Q7ZXXBAR) textbook and the complete public [Water and Wastewater Treatment Engineering — MIT 1.85](../sources/Water-and-Wastewater-Treatment-Engineering-MIT.lingua#r_396YEC55H29CR6J4ZBZX5JBY60) sequence. Later work the remaining biological-treatment volumes, all of [Biological Wastewater Treatment — Chen and colleagues, second edition](../sources/Biological-Wastewater-Treatment-Chen-and-Colleagues.lingua#r_1AE9DK0YWQR5GDECZ9KK1JJP37), [Assessment of Treatment Plant Performance and Water Quality Data — von Sperling, Verbyla and Oliveira](../sources/Treatment-Plant-Performance-and-Water-Quality-Data.lingua#r_5PZG8VN422GHD657FBDR5KRWGS) and [Industrial Water Treatment Operation and Maintenance — UFC 3-230-13](../sources/Industrial-Water-Treatment-UFC-3-230-13.lingua#r_41KNKBCA6GZWQ6VAJGAPG2HJ3R) in the directions specified by the studies. Public-health and legal sources accompany the engineering throughout, with their own dates and purposes. Keep an evolving account of one real supply and sanitation system as the reading deepens.

**Continue:** [A tap, a drain and the work between them](A-tap-a-drain-and-the-work-between-them.lingua#r_4BZY7VTHAE6B6WH956HKPZY906).

**Return:** [Water, sanitation and industrial utilities — from sources to continuing service](../Water-sanitation-and-industrial-utilities.lingua#r_7B9GRCJFHVBEEQEXKWCR2QMMPN).
